1
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:02,760
April sixteenth.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,440
Since the day the stall opened, Priya from

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,240
Infotech has taken chai for the whole floor,

4
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:09,280
every day.

5
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:10,700
On a tab.

6
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:12,280
Pay later.

7
00:00:12,831 --> 00:00:15,551
Today, Meera sends the first bill — two

8
00:00:15,631 --> 00:00:16,711
weeks of chai.

9
00:00:16,991 --> 00:00:18,511
Six thousand rupees.

10
00:00:18,751 --> 00:00:20,111
Her profit goes up.

11
00:00:20,431 --> 00:00:22,031
Her galla doesn't move.

12
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,080
So did Meera make money, or not?

13
00:00:32,307 --> 00:00:34,467
First, last time's answers.

14
00:00:34,787 --> 00:00:35,307
One.

15
00:00:35,587 --> 00:00:37,147
Is the cart an expense?

16
00:00:38,027 --> 00:00:38,427
No.

17
00:00:38,587 --> 00:00:41,347
It's still making chai, so it's an asset.

18
00:00:42,127 --> 00:00:42,607
Two.

19
00:00:42,847 --> 00:00:45,727
Meera's profit: eighteen thousand of revenue,

20
00:00:45,807 --> 00:00:47,807
minus five thousand of rent.

21
00:00:47,847 --> 00:00:49,487
Thirteen thousand rupees.

22
00:00:50,167 --> 00:00:50,887
Three.

23
00:00:51,087 --> 00:00:53,287
Profit lives on the right side of the scale,

24
00:00:53,527 --> 00:00:54,647
inside equity.

25
00:00:54,727 --> 00:00:56,007
It belongs to Meera.

26
00:00:57,073 --> 00:00:59,953
Today, Khata pins two needles on the stall's

27
00:01:00,113 --> 00:01:00,513
wall.

28
00:01:00,753 --> 00:01:02,193
The first is Profit.

29
00:01:02,593 --> 00:01:05,153
It moves when Meera earns money, or uses

30
00:01:05,193 --> 00:01:05,953
it up.

31
00:01:06,533 --> 00:01:08,973
The second is Money — everything in the

32
00:01:09,013 --> 00:01:11,333
galla, plus everything in the bank.

33
00:01:11,787 --> 00:01:14,747
Right now, profit reads thirteen thousand.

34
00:01:14,827 --> 00:01:17,147
Money reads fifty-one thousand.

35
00:01:17,227 --> 00:01:19,627
It's bigger, because it also holds Meera's

36
00:01:19,707 --> 00:01:21,467
savings and Ravi Mama's loan.

37
00:01:22,027 --> 00:01:23,787
Most people think these two needles move

38
00:01:23,867 --> 00:01:24,587
together.

39
00:01:24,827 --> 00:01:25,627
Let's watch.

40
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:28,440
First, rewind one day.

41
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:30,280
April fifteenth.

42
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:32,520
Meera carries fifteen thousand rupees from

43
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:33,920
the galla to the bank.

44
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:34,920
Profit?

45
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:36,360
No change.

46
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:36,960
Money?

47
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:38,480
Also no change.

48
00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:41,300
But in the books, these are two different

49
00:01:41,580 --> 00:01:42,060
accounts.

50
00:01:42,260 --> 00:01:44,180
Cash is the notes in the galla.

51
00:01:44,420 --> 00:01:46,660
Bank is money the bank keeps for her, and

52
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:48,500
gives back whenever she asks.

53
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:51,080
Cash went down fifteen thousand.

54
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:53,560
Bank went up fifteen thousand.

55
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:55,560
So the money needle doesn't move.

56
00:01:57,608 --> 00:01:59,648
Now, April sixteenth.

57
00:01:59,848 --> 00:02:00,968
Infotech's tab.

58
00:02:01,208 --> 00:02:02,888
Which two things changed?

59
00:02:04,858 --> 00:02:07,258
Sales went up by six thousand.

60
00:02:07,298 --> 00:02:09,578
The chai has been drunk, so Meera has earned

61
00:02:09,658 --> 00:02:10,218
it.

62
00:02:10,898 --> 00:02:13,298
But on the left, no money came in.

63
00:02:13,578 --> 00:02:16,178
Instead, Infotech now owes the stall six

64
00:02:16,258 --> 00:02:17,298
thousand rupees.

65
00:02:17,538 --> 00:02:20,178
Money that customers owe you is an asset,

66
00:02:20,338 --> 00:02:21,618
called a receivable.

67
00:02:22,076 --> 00:02:24,556
So the profit needle jumps, from thirteen

68
00:02:24,716 --> 00:02:26,876
thousand to nineteen thousand.

69
00:02:26,956 --> 00:02:27,956
And the money needle?

70
00:02:28,836 --> 00:02:30,356
It doesn't move at all.

71
00:02:31,964 --> 00:02:34,364
Revenue counts when it's earned — when the

72
00:02:34,524 --> 00:02:37,484
chai is drunk — not when the money arrives.

73
00:02:38,124 --> 00:02:40,244
And expenses count when they're incurred

74
00:02:40,564 --> 00:02:42,724
— when the thing is used up — not when they're

75
00:02:42,884 --> 00:02:43,524
paid.

76
00:02:44,304 --> 00:02:46,384
This idea is called accrual.

77
00:02:48,348 --> 00:02:49,868
April twentieth.

78
00:02:49,948 --> 00:02:52,348
Meera pays Gopal five thousand rupees of

79
00:02:52,428 --> 00:02:54,828
the eight thousand she owes him for milk.

80
00:02:54,908 --> 00:02:56,668
Meera's sure about this one.

81
00:02:56,748 --> 00:02:59,388
Money left the galla, so it's an expense.

82
00:03:00,005 --> 00:03:00,565
Nope.

83
00:03:00,805 --> 00:03:03,365
That milk came in as stock, and Gopal became

84
00:03:03,405 --> 00:03:04,565
a liability.

85
00:03:04,725 --> 00:03:07,525
Today, Meera is only paying down that debt.

86
00:03:07,605 --> 00:03:08,965
So which needle moves?

87
00:03:10,936 --> 00:03:12,456
Only the money needle.

88
00:03:12,696 --> 00:03:14,136
Down five thousand.

89
00:03:14,336 --> 00:03:16,536
Profit stays at nineteen thousand.

90
00:03:17,076 --> 00:03:19,356
The payment shrinks a liability.

91
00:03:20,076 --> 00:03:22,436
Money the stall owes a supplier is a payable

92
00:03:22,836 --> 00:03:24,676
— the mirror of a receivable.

93
00:03:25,927 --> 00:03:27,527
April twenty-second.

94
00:03:27,607 --> 00:03:29,447
A customer pays four thousand rupees in

95
00:03:29,527 --> 00:03:32,487
advance, for a catering order on May fifth.

96
00:03:33,027 --> 00:03:34,347
Meera's quick this time.

97
00:03:34,587 --> 00:03:35,787
Money in from a customer?

98
00:03:36,187 --> 00:03:38,747
Revenue — straight into the profit pocket.

99
00:03:39,664 --> 00:03:40,184
Nope.

100
00:03:40,384 --> 00:03:42,504
Meera hasn't made a single cup yet.

101
00:03:42,704 --> 00:03:44,864
Until May fifth, she owes that customer

102
00:03:44,944 --> 00:03:47,264
an event — or their money back.

103
00:03:47,804 --> 00:03:50,404
An advance is a liability, not revenue.

104
00:03:50,724 --> 00:03:51,604
Not yet.

105
00:03:52,444 --> 00:03:54,204
Meera, which needle moves?

106
00:03:56,162 --> 00:03:57,842
Only the money needle.

107
00:03:57,962 --> 00:03:59,362
Up four thousand.

108
00:03:59,562 --> 00:04:01,682
Profit stays at nineteen thousand.

109
00:04:02,948 --> 00:04:04,788
Now you, on your own.

110
00:04:05,108 --> 00:04:06,628
April twenty-fifth.

111
00:04:06,748 --> 00:04:08,788
Infotech pays four thousand rupees of its

112
00:04:08,868 --> 00:04:10,748
tab, by UPI.

113
00:04:11,028 --> 00:04:11,748
Profit?

114
00:04:12,588 --> 00:04:13,228
Money?

115
00:04:16,387 --> 00:04:18,947
Money goes up by four thousand — straight

116
00:04:19,027 --> 00:04:19,747
into the bank.

117
00:04:19,907 --> 00:04:21,627
The galla never even sees it.

118
00:04:22,227 --> 00:04:23,587
Profit doesn't move.

119
00:04:23,827 --> 00:04:26,667
Meera earned that money back on April sixteenth.

120
00:04:26,867 --> 00:04:28,747
Today, she's only collecting it.

121
00:04:29,447 --> 00:04:32,407
The receivable shrinks, and the bank grows.

122
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:35,980
Since April fifteenth, the profit needle

123
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:39,140
moved once — on the day no money came in.

124
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:42,340
The money needle moved three times — and

125
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:44,260
not one of those was profit.

126
00:04:44,812 --> 00:04:47,372
Profit: nineteen thousand rupees.

127
00:04:47,612 --> 00:04:49,932
Money: fifty-four thousand.

128
00:04:50,612 --> 00:04:51,732
Two needles.

129
00:04:51,812 --> 00:04:53,172
Two different stories.

130
00:04:53,918 --> 00:04:57,198
Cash basis counts money only when it moves.

131
00:04:57,818 --> 00:05:00,418
Accrual basis counts revenue when it's earned,

132
00:05:00,458 --> 00:05:02,658
and expenses when they're incurred.

133
00:05:03,438 --> 00:05:05,598
Businesses use accrual, because it shows

134
00:05:05,678 --> 00:05:07,758
what was really earned — even while the

135
00:05:07,838 --> 00:05:09,358
money is still on its way.

136
00:05:10,629 --> 00:05:12,309
So — two needles.

137
00:05:12,549 --> 00:05:15,029
Earned isn't the same as received.

138
00:05:15,269 --> 00:05:17,589
Paid isn't the same as used up.

139
00:05:17,989 --> 00:05:20,069
Profit is not cash.

140
00:05:21,213 --> 00:05:21,893
Your turn.

141
00:05:22,093 --> 00:05:23,093
Three quick ones.

142
00:05:23,293 --> 00:05:23,773
One.

143
00:05:24,013 --> 00:05:25,933
The four-thousand-rupee catering advance

144
00:05:26,253 --> 00:05:27,613
— is it revenue in April?

145
00:05:28,093 --> 00:05:28,533
Two.

146
00:05:28,733 --> 00:05:31,133
Paying Gopal — is that an expense?

147
00:05:33,173 --> 00:05:33,733
Three.

148
00:05:33,973 --> 00:05:36,693
After the UPI payment, how much does Infotech

149
00:05:36,773 --> 00:05:37,813
still owe Meera?

150
00:05:39,853 --> 00:05:42,013
Answers at the start of the next lesson.

151
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:45,354
And now — Checkpoint two.

152
00:05:45,594 --> 00:05:47,434
Back to Aman's samosa cart.

153
00:05:47,554 --> 00:05:48,714
Five things happen.

154
00:05:48,794 --> 00:05:50,874
For each one, write down what it does to

155
00:05:51,114 --> 00:05:52,874
profit, and to cash.

156
00:05:53,335 --> 00:05:53,935
One.

157
00:05:54,135 --> 00:05:56,695
Cash sales of nine thousand rupees.

158
00:05:56,855 --> 00:05:57,335
Two.

159
00:05:57,415 --> 00:06:00,135
He pays two thousand rupees of stall rent.

160
00:06:00,295 --> 00:06:00,775
Three.

161
00:06:00,855 --> 00:06:02,935
He supplies a school canteen with fifteen

162
00:06:03,015 --> 00:06:05,655
hundred rupees of samosas, on credit.

163
00:06:05,735 --> 00:06:06,375
Four.

164
00:06:06,455 --> 00:06:09,255
He pays Sharma Kirana two thousand rupees.

165
00:06:09,495 --> 00:06:10,055
Five.

166
00:06:10,135 --> 00:06:12,455
A customer gives him a thousand-rupee advance,

167
00:06:12,495 --> 00:06:14,375
for a birthday party next month.

168
00:06:14,495 --> 00:06:16,935
Pause the video now, and try all five.

169
00:06:20,097 --> 00:06:20,497
Ready?

170
00:06:20,977 --> 00:06:21,457
One.

171
00:06:21,697 --> 00:06:23,537
Nine thousand of cash sales.

172
00:06:23,697 --> 00:06:26,737
Profit and cash both go up nine thousand.

173
00:06:26,817 --> 00:06:27,457
Two.

174
00:06:27,497 --> 00:06:29,297
Two thousand of stall rent.

175
00:06:29,417 --> 00:06:31,377
Both go down two thousand.

176
00:06:31,537 --> 00:06:32,017
Three.

177
00:06:32,057 --> 00:06:33,937
Fifteen hundred of samosas to the school

178
00:06:34,017 --> 00:06:35,297
canteen, on credit.

179
00:06:35,697 --> 00:06:37,457
Profit up fifteen hundred.

180
00:06:37,657 --> 00:06:38,977
Cash, nothing.

181
00:06:39,057 --> 00:06:39,377
Four.

182
00:06:39,697 --> 00:06:41,857
Paying Sharma Kirana two thousand.

183
00:06:42,017 --> 00:06:43,537
Cash down two thousand.

184
00:06:43,737 --> 00:06:46,417
Profit, nothing — it's a debt being paid.

185
00:06:46,897 --> 00:06:47,617
Five.

186
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:49,577
The thousand-rupee birthday advance.

187
00:06:49,777 --> 00:06:51,457
Cash up one thousand.

188
00:06:51,657 --> 00:06:53,777
Profit, nothing — it isn't earned yet.

189
00:06:54,777 --> 00:06:57,337
Aman's profit so far: eight thousand five

190
00:06:57,417 --> 00:06:58,377
hundred rupees.

191
00:06:59,888 --> 00:07:02,568
Next time — remember that bank deposit?

192
00:07:03,448 --> 00:07:05,048
Meera's phone buzzed.

193
00:07:05,128 --> 00:07:07,528
Your account is credited with fifteen thousand

194
00:07:07,608 --> 00:07:08,408
rupees.

195
00:07:08,448 --> 00:07:09,528
Credited!

196
00:07:09,688 --> 00:07:11,208
Great news… right?
